        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: रुग्ण",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "रुग्ण — rugṇa — \"a sick person; a patient\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दवाखान्यात सकाळपासून रुग्णांची रांग होती. davākhānyāt sakāḷpāsūn rugṇāñcī rāṅg hotī. There was a queue of patients at the clinic from the morning."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "As in रुग्णालय, a hospital, and रुग्णवाहिका, an ambulance."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "रुग्ण (rugṇa) is a tatsama, taken from Sanskrit rugṇa, \"broken, diseased\" (CDIAL 10760)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
